// Argent has no macros, so tools/router-gen/gen-router.sh writes the 30
// actors out. KasToToken_buy, _buy_out, _buy3, TokenToKas_sell2,
// TokenSwap_swap and _swap2_out show every ingredient.
//
// POSITIONAL ANTI-ALIASING RULE. Argent generates none, so this one is
// hand-written and reviewed. The intent spent at input j owns exactly two
// outputs, j and j + 1, and everything it owes goes there.
//     KasToToken  out j = payer KAS change      out j+1 = merchant delivery
//     TokenToKas  out j = merchant KAS          out j+1 = payer token change
//     TokenSwap   out j = merchant delivery (B) out j+1 = payer change (A)
// Output j+1 is the last output of the token group the intent observes.
// Output j is checked by index, and in TokenSwap it is the last output of the
// token B group. An order pays, delivers or refunds at its own input index,
// so the intent must be the last input (tx.inputs.length == j + 1).
// Otherwise an unobserved bid of the merchant or payer at j + 1 could take
// the router's token output as its delivery, and an observed ask's refund
// could take it as its return. So no output can serve two rules. Two intents
// cannot share a delivery, and a self-trading payer cannot make one output
